{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1405187-an-extremely-silly-idea-i-had-regarding-autochthonians-and-music","id":1405187,"title":"An extremely silly idea I had regarding Autochthonians and music.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-29T12:34:08-07:00","id":1405187,"title":"An extremely silly idea I had regarding Autochthonians and music.","content":"I've never actually <i>been</i> in an Exalted game except a 2e game that blew up after one session (which I had to leave halfway in too) in like 2012 but I'm still a fan of the series if only for the lore and just the wonderful feel of it compared to most RPG's. Well, I am a writer, and I do have this sort of...&quot;head-game&quot; running in my head with a bunch of Exalted...&quot;OC's&quot; one could call them? I have never written it down, as Exalted fanfic is not really a thing, and it'd be insanely super long, but I do like plotting it out and coming up with the characters when I'm ADHD-daydreaming.<br /> <br /> Now this game is intentionally a bit silly and tongue-in-cheek while remaining mostly serious. Think Keychain of Creation which really does influence my view of how I'd write an Exalted story heavily. One particular result of this is a Chosen of Endings in this story of mine, who spent a bit too much time in the Wyld and therefore accidentally got...mind-teleported (it's vague) to the Modern Shard and stumbled upon a bunch of metal and hardcore punk concerts, which left <i>such</i> an impact on her that she turned her heavenly manse into a literal rock stadium and wields a starmetal &quot;axe&quot; that's also doubles as an electric guitar. Most in Yu-shan think it to be unlistenable noise, but a few young sidereal and gods are oddly interested...<br /> <br /> Now, in this story, Autochthonia re-establishes contact with Creation, thankfully nearby the Eclipse Caste main character's fledgeling kindgom, and things go mostly peacefully. Except this Endings caste <i>also</i> went into Autochthonia, and mostly by accident introduced them (Claslat only at first as they breached and are dealing with our Eclipse caste here) to this kind of music. With our Eclipse and his pet Twilight using their Solar Hax to make Claslat more efficient, the Populat suddenly found them with a bit more free time, and hey, in a place like Autochthonia, guitars shouldn't be too hard to build, and the aggressive tones of metal and punk music are absolutely more suited to the Realm of Brass and Shadow than it is Creation...<br /> <br /> So now Autochthonia is grappling with the fact that a single Sidereal accidentally made punk and metal a thing for the younger populat, who are increasingly spending what precious free time they have going to shows and forming bands (the fact that said music actually frankly talks about the troubles plaguing autochthonians instead of being propaganda helps, and exposure to Creation has meant that many Populat are more receptive to novel things), and I just really find this to be an incredibly amusing idea. Can you imagine a Lector <i>literally</i> <i>Tome-of-the-Great-Maker</i>-thumping against this sinful &quot;void music&quot;? One of the Alchemical characters in this story actually joins a band himself (the novelty of a Champion singing about the exact same kinds of human emotions and troubles that a regular Populat member shares in has made him quite popular. Performing emotional music to a crowd definitely has to reduce Clarity, right?)!<br /> <br /> I just had to bring this up. I'm a fan of being a bit silly with Creation and its associated worlds, much like KoC was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 07-29-2020, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T18:31:57-07:00","id":1521846,"title":"","content":"Nice to see other interpretations on Autochthonia and Music, I liked this post =)<br /> <br /> I always tought that musical instruments in the realm of brass and shadow would be more &quot;metallic&quot; or experimental.... pending to Eletronic Music or Industrial Techno and not &quot;Punk/Metal &quot;.<br /> <br /> My personal interpretation makes me to think that Punk music leads to uprising and brings power to the people... thats a powerfull musical style to move revolutions - Rage Against the Machine vibes. Some Regulators might think that's not appropriate music LOL. (Don't get me wrong I love punk rock). Maybe in renegade cities in the Reaches, Punk Music is the main attraction. =)<br /> <br /> I can imagine bands with pseudo-technological instruments like Steel Drums, Stylophone, Theremin, Pipe Xylophones, Musical Saw, Steel Flutes and so on playing Industrial Techno Music. &quot;<br /> &quot;This kinda music is focused on repetition, cadence that might lead to &quot;more efficiency&quot;. - Words said by an Olgatory Member. <br /> <br /> Just sharing other point of view.... I really liked your StarMetal Axe-Guitar Artifact =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you like Alchemicals, please check out my DeviantArt Gallery!! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> - 5 Magic Materials BeamKlaves and Gyroscopic Chakrans ? OK<br /> - Autochthonia updated World Map? OK<br /> And many more! <a href=\"http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals\" target=\"_blank\">http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals</a>","edited":